                { author: "Matt", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-22", text: "Firstly it was really difficult - I’ve run ultramarathons and have climbed one other 3,000m+ peak and this was up there in difficulty. Part of the challenge was not having the right equipment - you need a big bag to carry 3L+ of water and huge snack/lunch boxes. You could really do with specialist climbing/hiking shoes thatre good with slippy volcanic rock. And cold weather and rain protection gear is a must. The tour should do more to let you know about this before the trip." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-25", text: "Le guide était génial et l’écoute, la vue était époustouflante. Je recommande fortement attention toutefois la montée s’avère rude par moment et il faut être patient pour la descente! 10/10!" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 2, date: "2025-08-25", text: "The sunrise was spectacular but we found this activity to be quite poorly planned overall. We were picked up from hour hotel at 9:30 pm and driven to the start of the hike, where we met our guide, who spoke no English. We were given a very basic breakfast for the following morning. Despite having asked in advance for vegan food, the only vegan elements were 2 bananas. We were told we should bring our own food. The hike up was smooth until we stopped at around 2600m and waited for two hours in the cold, to avoid reaching the summit way before sunrise. We found this nonsensical as there are more" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2025-08-05", text: "Mount Agung was perfect and it was really pretty, but the guide we got wasn’t the best! He was not bad and he made his job, but he was going to quickly, my friends and felt that he just wanted to end the job as quickly as he could, but other than that it was a really cool experience!" }
