                { author: "Travis", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-06-12", text: "Narta was extremely nice and knowledgeable about the area and how it fit with the Jujutsu Kaisen story. He was very interested in our thoughts about JJK and Anime in general and shared his as well. Our teenagers bonded with Narta as we traversed the scenes of the Shibuya Incident & Gojo vs Sukuna. We were able to see side by side images from the show/manga with the actual locations, which showed the great detail put into the production. It was an amazing experience. We highly recommend this tour to any JJK fans as we would not have been able to find and appreciate the exact locations on our ow" },
                { author: "Naveen", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-26", text: "The tour was great. the tour guide was very intelligible in JJK and I would highly recommend this for any hard-core JJK fan." },
                { author: "Neil", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-20", text: "It was excellent and the guide was very knowledgeable and came prepared with everything you could want. It’s a must for any JJK fan in Tokyo. Bring your walking shoes!! Thanks for the great tour mate" },
                { author: "Amy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-18", text: "This ended up being the highlight of my whole Tokyo trip as a JJK fan! If you’ve seen the Shibuya Incident arc, the first half is already amazing. And if you’ve read manga vols. 25 and 26, the second half becomes an even better Gojo experience. Narta brought printed scene photos, which made it really easy to match the anime/manga to the real locations. In Shibuya, I even got to film one of those angle-matching videos like the ones that went viral on TikTok. Super recommended for JJK fans." },
                { author: "Aida", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-21", text: "Моему сыну экскурсия очень понравилась, наш гид все показал, рассказал, сопровождал все виды соответствующими фото и советовал как лучше сделать фото. Отдельно спасибо нашему гиду за его терпение! Не смотря на жаркую погоду, для нас эскурсия прошла очень легко и непринужденно! Сын сказал, что не заметил, как время быстро пролетело! Спасибо за все!" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-20", text: "Tokyo was already exciting in general, but as a JJK fan, this was probably the most fun thing I did there. I’m a big Gojo fan, and the guide was really flexible when I said I wanted to spend a bit more time at the Gojo-related spots. Getting a bunch of Prison Realm photos when there weren’t many people around was honestly one of the best parts. The guide was super prepared and somehow got us through maze-like Shibuya and Shinjuku really smoothly. Taking real photos while holding up the anime scene prints he brought was insanely cool. He also shared a Google Maps list for official JJK merch, wh" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-12", text: "I joined this tour during some free time in Tokyo, and as a huge JJK and anime fan, it ended up being one of the best things I did there. I like a lot of characters, but Gojo is definitely one of my favorites, and I had already read the manga up to volume 29. So being able to walk around the real Shinjuku locations from Gojo vs. Sukuna was honestly amazing. Narta even brought the English manga volumes, and seeing that final panel in the actual place almost got me emotional haha. I also enjoyed the more classic side of Japan, like the traditional beauty of Kyoto and the scenery around Mt. Fuji," }
