                { author: "Barbara", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-29", text: "The class started with the fitting of a samurai suit. The staff was very attentive and helped with getting dressed in the traditional garments. After that we started the class and learned how to draw the sword, and different forms of attacks and how to holster the sword again. We learned the movements with the fan and even practiced a small choreography. After our class was over our sensei Hisyo took pictures in different poses for us. The Kenbu show at the end of the class was very impressive and enjoyable to watch. As as side note: as a bigger person I had issues in the past with these fitti" },
                { author: "Chris", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-28", text: "As a family we were so impressed how inclusive the session was. The instructors were excellent. They were friendly, fun and patient. I would highly recommend this for families. We were in a group of ten some together and others alone but the session was aimed at inclusivity and teamwork. We learnt so much about the culture and history of the Samurai." },
                { author: "Barbara", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-15", text: "This was a very enjoyable experience overall. It was interactive and felt like actual samurai training, which made it both fun and memorable. My only suggestions would be to slow down the pace a little and reduce the group size, as there were many participants and it sometimes felt rushed. I also wish there had been more costume options available. That said, I had a great time and would recommend it to anyone looking for a unique cultural experience. For younger children under 10, it may be a bit less suitable." },
                { author: "Monica", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-06-23", text: "This was a A+ family friendly experience! We got to dress in costumes and learn traditional sword and fan dances. Our teacher was very knowledgeable, funny, and assisted with pictures for our family." }
